#######################################################################
# test_Poisson_2D.cases
#
# What each output of test_Poisson_2D.lgi is, so that
# run_test_poisson_2d.sh can check it. The deck itself is not edited.
#
# One line per output file written by the deck:
#
#   output    the file the deck dumps
#   polygon   the polygon it was meshed from
#   h0        the h given on the createpts line (POI_H_FACTOR)
#   field     uniform | absx      (see check_test_poisson_2d.py)
#   width     WIDTH_FACTOR for absx, - for uniform
#   verify    a field file dumped by user_h_field_att.mlgi to check
#             this case's formula against, or -
#
# Only the LAST variable run's h_field_out.inp survives, because the
# .mlgi dumps every run to the same file name, so only that case
# carries a verify file.
#
# If the deck changes, change this file to match.
#######################################################################
# output                          polygon           h0    field   width verify
output01_unit_square_uniform.inp  unit_square.poly  0.05  uniform -     -
output02_unit_square_var.inp      unit_square.poly  0.01  absx    10    -
output03_unit_square_var.inp      unit_square.poly  0.01  absx    20    h_field_out.inp
